title: m1_trade_content
---

Virtual Instructor: This is the carpentry zone. Carpenters perform a variety of tasks involving awkward postures.

Virtual Instructor: See how the worker cutting timber is bending the wrists repeatedly? This increases wrist strain.

Virtual Instructor: Overhead beam installation puts heavy stress on the shoulder and neck.

Virtual Instructor: Stud framing close to the floor forces the worker into a deep squat, raising back and knee risk.

Virtual Instructor: Try assessing the risk for this worker!

